# Context

## Background
Workstream 1 of plans/2026-11-09-upstream-alignment.md: editor parity
ported from upstream lawn (7d066eb, da3d9cd, 184c352), closing two
long-standing items on todo.md (Final Cut keybindings, theater mode).

## Why This Way
- shuttle.ts is a byte-identical upstream port (zero imports, no Mux
  coupling); the shortcut BINDER was refactored into a handle-based
  module with the K-chord state machine extracted for unit tests.
  Upstream's in-file binder copy was deleted so the chord logic exists
  once (review finding).
- Watch-minute billing is rate-scaled (delta / max(1, |rate|)) because
  this fork meters team watch caps upstream does not have; without
  scaling, 32x skim review billed content time and could lock out the
  whole workspace mid-review. Reverse playback bills nothing (backward
  deltas are ignored by design).
- Default playback source flipped from the original-source presign
  (600 s signed GET of the full-res MP4) to the Mux 720p session via
  dashboardPlaybackSource.ts; bf041bd frozen-video recovery deferred as
  inapplicable under forced-720p signed manifests - revisit if
  original-source stalls are reported.

## Gotchas
- Frame stepping assumes 30 fps (upstream default); 24/25 fps media
  needs a frameRate plumbed through.
- The INTERACTIVE selector is duplicated across shuttle.ts,
  bindPlaybackShortcuts.ts, and VideoEditorLayout.tsx (accepted
  port-phase artifact; consolidate on next touch).
- Escape-closes-menus relies on React child-before-parent effect order:
  the player's listener registers before VideoEditorLayout's theater
  listener, so preventDefault blocks theater over an open menu.
- 16x/32x seek-driven playback fires ~30 seeks/s; manual QA against a
  real signed manifest is still recommended before wide use.

